asr-000043
00:03:23.890 --> 00:03:25.650
Rep. Alexandria "Queenie" Gonzales: Thank you, ComSec.

asr-000044
00:03:26.010 --> 00:03:29.450
Rep. Alexandria "Queenie" Gonzales: So, distinguished colleagues, honorable members of the committee,

asr-000045
00:03:29.730 --> 00:03:36.170
Rep. Alexandria "Queenie" Gonzales: officials of the Presidential Communications Office and its attached agencies and corporations,

asr-000046
00:03:36.710 --> 00:03:39.030
Rep. Alexandria "Queenie" Gonzales: our resource persons, and distinguished guests,

asr-000047
00:03:39.410 --> 00:03:41.810
Rep. Alexandria "Queenie" Gonzales: magandang hapon po sa ating lahat.

asr-000048
00:03:42.270 --> 00:03:46.670
Rep. Alexandria "Queenie" Gonzales: Today's budget hearing gives the committee an opportunity to examine

asr-000049
00:03:46.670 --> 00:03:53.990
Rep. Alexandria "Queenie" Gonzales: how the Presidential Communications Office fulfills one of the government's

asr-000050
00:03:54.890 --> 00:03:59.870
Rep. Alexandria "Queenie" Gonzales: most fundamental responsibilities,

asr-000051
00:03:59.870 --> 00:04:04.170
Rep. Alexandria "Queenie" Gonzales: keeping the people accurately, promptly, and meaningfully informed.

asr-000052
00:04:04.710 --> 00:04:09.130
Rep. Alexandria "Queenie" Gonzales: Under Executive Order No. 16, Series of 2023,

asr-000053
00:04:09.470 --> 00:04:16.230
Rep. Alexandria "Queenie" Gonzales: the PCO serves as the communication arm of the Executive Branch,

asr-000054
00:04:16.230 --> 00:04:19.750
Rep. Alexandria "Queenie" Gonzales: responsible for formulating, coordinating, and implementing integrated public information programs

asr-000055
00:04:19.750 --> 00:04:22.490
Rep. Alexandria "Queenie" Gonzales: concerning the policies, programs, and activities of the President and the National Government.

asr-000058
00:04:22.490 --> 00:04:25.930
Rep. Alexandria "Queenie" Gonzales: This function is essential to effective governance.

asr-000059
00:04:26.430 --> 00:04:33.790
Rep. Alexandria "Queenie" Gonzales: Government programs can serve the public only when citizens understand what assistance is available,

asr-000060
00:04:34.290 --> 00:04:41.350
Rep. Alexandria "Queenie" Gonzales: how to access it, why policies are being adopted, and how public institutions may be held accountable.

asr-000061
00:04:41.350 --> 00:04:46.650
Rep. Alexandria "Queenie" Gonzales: Clear communication, therefore, connects policy with public service,

asr-000062
00:04:46.990 --> 00:04:51.150
Rep. Alexandria "Queenie" Gonzales: supports participation, and helps sustain trust,

asr-000063
00:04:51.150 --> 00:04:53.790
Rep. Alexandria "Queenie" Gonzales: between the government and the people.

asr-000064
00:04:54.190 --> 00:04:58.130
Rep. Alexandria "Queenie" Gonzales: This responsibility has become even more significant at a time

asr-000065
00:04:58.130 --> 00:05:01.830
Rep. Alexandria "Queenie" Gonzales: when social media is woven into everyday life.

asr-000066
00:05:01.830 --> 00:05:05.350
Rep. Alexandria "Queenie" Gonzales: Information now reaches millions within seconds,

asr-000067
00:05:05.490 --> 00:05:13.590
Rep. Alexandria "Queenie" Gonzales: but so do misinformation, disinformation, manipulated content, and AI-generated material.

asr-000068
00:05:14.260 --> 00:05:19.610
Rep. Alexandria "Queenie" Gonzales: The PCO must be present where people receive and exchange information,

asr-000069
00:05:19.890 --> 00:05:22.790
Rep. Alexandria "Queenie" Gonzales: not merely to broadcast official messages,

asr-000070
00:05:23.170 --> 00:06:30.010
Rep. Alexandria "Queenie" Gonzales: but to communicate quickly, clearly, credibly, and directly affect the daily lives of the Filipinos.

asr-000071
00:06:30.010 --> 00:06:35.770
Rep. Alexandria "Queenie" Gonzales: The total budget of the PCO and its attached agencies and corporations

asr-000072
00:06:35.770 --> 00:06:42.870
Rep. Alexandria "Queenie" Gonzales: was 2.768 billion under the fiscal year 2026 NEP

asr-000073
00:06:42.870 --> 00:06:50.450
Rep. Alexandria "Queenie" Gonzales: and is proposed at 2.621 billion under the fiscal year 2027 NEP.

asr-000076
00:06:50.450 --> 00:06:57.370
Rep. Alexandria "Queenie" Gonzales: We look forward to a productive discussion on the PCO's fiscal year 2026 performance

asr-000077
00:06:57.370 --> 00:07:05.050
Rep. Alexandria "Queenie" Gonzales: and on the concrete outputs, safeguards, and measurable results to be delivered under its fiscal year 2027 proposal.

asr-000078
00:07:05.830 --> 00:07:13.750
Rep. Alexandria "Queenie" Gonzales: Our objective is to support a communication system that informs rather than confuses, engages rather than excludes,

asr-000079
00:07:13.750 --> 00:07:19.250
Rep. Alexandria "Queenie" Gonzales: and strengthens the people's trust in government through truth, clarity, and accountability.

asr-000080
00:07:19.250 --> 00:07:20.730
Rep. Alexandria "Queenie" Gonzales: Thank you and good afternoon.

asr-000081
00:07:22.860 --> 00:07:27.720
Rep. Alexandria "Queenie" Gonzales: Secretary Dave Gomez, sir, you may now proceed with your presentation.

asr-000082
00:07:32.030 --> 00:07:38.190
Secretary David M. Gomez: Thank you very much and good afternoon, Madam Chair, Honorable Members of the House Committee on Appropriations.

asr-000083
00:07:38.810 --> 00:07:45.410
Secretary David M. Gomez: On behalf of the Presidential Communications Office, let me express our gratitude for the gracious invitation today

asr-000084
00:07:45.410 --> 00:07:49.790
Secretary David M. Gomez: and for the very warm welcome to the August halls of the House of Representatives.

asr-000085
00:07:50.510 --> 00:07:56.310
Secretary David M. Gomez: It will be my honor, together with the heads and officials of the PCO and our attached agencies,

asr-000086
00:07:56.530 --> 00:08:02.830
Secretary David M. Gomez: to present and explain the rationale behind our proposed budget for fiscal year 2027.

asr-000087
00:08:03.670 --> 00:08:12.630
Secretary David M. Gomez: But before I proceed, Madam Chair, allow me to simply frame the context of our proposed 2027 appropriations.

asr-000088
00:08:12.630 --> 00:08:25.750
Secretary David M. Gomez: The PCO is proposing a budget of 2.62 billion pesos, which is 6.6% lower than our current 2026 budget.

asr-000089
00:08:26.250 --> 00:08:35.130
Secretary David M. Gomez: This represents a measly 0.03% of the total 7.2 trillion proposed national budget.

asr-000090
00:08:35.770 --> 00:08:43.470
Secretary David M. Gomez: We have the lowest budget and the last department-level agency of the Executive Department in terms of budgetary allocation.

asr-000091
00:08:44.410 --> 00:08:56.010
Secretary David M. Gomez: We may have the least in the budget priority, but we assure your honors that the PCO and our attached agencies are up to the Herculean task of engaging and involving the citizenry,

asr-000092
00:08:56.010 --> 00:09:02.590
Secretary David M. Gomez: and the mass media in enriching the quality of public discourse on all matters of governance.

asr-000093
00:09:03.690 --> 00:09:04.550
Secretary David M. Gomez: Next slide, please.

asr-000094
00:09:05.570 --> 00:09:22.370
Secretary David M. Gomez: As I have just mentioned, the PCO family's budget proposal is 2.62 billion pesos, or around 0.03% of the 7.2 trillion national expenditure program for fiscal year 2027.

asr-000095
00:09:23.400 --> 00:09:25.970
Secretary David M. Gomez: And it is 6.6% lower.

asr-000096
00:09:25.970 --> 00:09:29.450
Secretary David M. Gomez: than the 2026 current level of our budget.

asr-000097
00:09:29.450 --> 00:09:45.390
Secretary David M. Gomez: Just very quickly, as per Executive Order No. 16, you will see that the PCO has six attached agencies and three GOCCs that are also attached to the PCO.

asr-000098
00:09:45.510 --> 00:09:55.750
Secretary David M. Gomez: They are the Bureau of Broadcast Services, the Bureau of Communication Services, the News and Information Bureau, the Philippine Information Agency, Radio TV Malacanang or RTVM,

asr-000099
00:09:55.890 --> 00:09:59.090
Secretary David M. Gomez: IBC 13, PTV 4, APO Press, and the Philippine Information Agency.

asr-000100
00:09:59.090 --> 00:10:01.070
Secretary David M. Gomez: We have the EPO, the Program of Production, and the National Printing Office.

asr-000101
00:10:04.160 --> 00:10:11.560
Secretary David M. Gomez: Here, the following are the major programs, activities, and projects to be funded by our proposed fiscal year 2027 budget.

asr-000102
00:10:14.350 --> 00:10:20.390
Secretary David M. Gomez: As Madam Chair pointed out, the highest in terms of our priorities, the Presidential Communications Program,

asr-000103
00:10:21.230 --> 00:10:25.730
Secretary David M. Gomez: is at the core of our mandate to serve as the primary communications arm of the Executive Department,

asr-000104
00:10:26.150 --> 00:10:31.510
Secretary David M. Gomez: ensuring that government messages are clear, consistent, and accessible to the Filipino people.

asr-000117
00:10:33.130 --> 00:10:46.910
Secretary David M. Gomez: It focuses on the formulation, coordination, and implementation of integrated public information plans and programs that effectively communicate the priorities, policies, and achievements of the President and the Philippine Government.

asr-000118
00:10:47.210 --> 00:11:00.850
Secretary David M. Gomez: It not only involves the crafting of messages, but also the careful alignment of communication strategies across all agencies to ensure coherence, clarity in how government policies and programs are conveyed to the public.

asr-000119
00:11:01.510 --> 00:11:12.470
Secretary David M. Gomez: In a time when information is fast-moving and often contested, the program ensures that our citizens receive timely, accurate, and relevant information straight from the government.

asr-000120
00:11:12.770 --> 00:11:23.550
Secretary David M. Gomez: It is anchored on our sector outcome, which is people-centered, innovative, clean, efficient, effective, and inclusive delivery of public goods and services.

asr-000121
00:11:24.310 --> 00:11:28.990
Secretary David M. Gomez: Strategic communications plays a vital role in realizing this outcome.

asr-000122
00:11:28.990 --> 00:11:30.890
Secretary David M. Gomez: By delivering clear,

asr-000123
00:11:31.130 --> 00:11:43.550
Secretary David M. Gomez: reliable information, we strengthen transparency and accountability in governance, while ensuring that services and programs are better understood and appreciated by the people they are intended to serve.

asr-000124
00:11:43.810 --> 00:11:54.970
Secretary David M. Gomez: Communication, therefore, becomes a tool not only for information sharing, but also for enabling citizens to fully benefit from government programs and participate in the democratic process.

asr-000125
00:11:55.750 --> 00:12:00.230
Secretary David M. Gomez: In line with this, the organizational outcome that we seek to achieve in public access,

asr-000126
00:12:00.510 --> 00:12:01.430
Secretary David M. Gomez: engagement, and participation in the democratic process,

asr-000127
00:12:01.430 --> 00:12:04.610
Secretary David M. Gomez: and understanding of presidential policies and government programs.

asr-000128
00:12:04.830 --> 00:12:14.150
Secretary David M. Gomez: This means that we are not only ensuring that information reaches the people, but also that it resonates with them and encourages meaningful dialogue.

asr-000129
00:12:14.970 --> 00:12:23.830
Secretary David M. Gomez: Through accessible and inclusive communication, we empower citizens to engage in public discourse, to raise their concerns, and to take part in nation-building.

asr-000130
00:12:23.830 --> 00:12:34.030
Secretary David M. Gomez: In doing so, the program fosters a deeper appreciation of government initiatives and helps bridge the gap between policy formulation and citizen experience.

asr-000137
00:12:35.370 --> 00:12:39.490
Secretary David M. Gomez: To realize these outcomes, we are implementing several concrete activities.

asr-000138
00:12:39.890 --> 00:12:48.010
Secretary David M. Gomez: Among this is the freedom of information program, which upholds transparency by granting citizens greater access to government data and information.

asr-000139
00:12:48.010 --> 00:12:55.670
Secretary David M. Gomez: We also conduct regular press briefings to provide timely updates and clarifications on the president's directives and government initiatives.

asr-000140
00:12:56.530 --> 00:13:00.770
Secretary David M. Gomez: To strengthen information literacy, we have launched the Maging Mapanuri

asr-000141
00:13:00.770 --> 00:13:02.950
Secretary David M. Gomez: program, a series of fact-checking

asr-000142
00:13:02.950 --> 00:13:04.790
Secretary David M. Gomez: workshops designed to combat disinformation

asr-000143
00:13:04.790 --> 00:13:06.670
Secretary David M. Gomez: and promote responsible

asr-000144
00:13:06.670 --> 00:13:08.390
Secretary David M. Gomez: news consumption. We

asr-000145
00:13:08.390 --> 00:13:10.410
Secretary David M. Gomez: likewise provide various communication

asr-000146
00:13:10.410 --> 00:13:12.970
Secretary David M. Gomez: workshops and capability-building activities

asr-000147
00:13:12.970 --> 00:13:14.290
Secretary David M. Gomez: for state media

asr-000148
00:13:14.290 --> 00:13:16.570
Secretary David M. Gomez: and the covering media, enhancing

asr-000149
00:13:16.570 --> 00:13:18.470
Secretary David M. Gomez: their skills in messaging, crisis

asr-000150
00:13:18.470 --> 00:13:20.070
Secretary David M. Gomez: communications, and innovative

asr-000151
00:13:20.070 --> 00:13:22.630
Secretary David M. Gomez: content delivery. The program

asr-000152
00:13:22.630 --> 00:13:24.630
Secretary David M. Gomez: also undertakes the coverage

asr-000153
00:13:24.630 --> 00:13:26.550
Secretary David M. Gomez: of presidential engagements, both

asr-000154
00:13:26.550 --> 00:13:28.790
Secretary David M. Gomez: local and international, ensuring

asr-000155
00:13:28.790 --> 00:13:30.670
Secretary David M. Gomez: that the Filipino people are kept

asr-000156
00:13:30.670 --> 00:13:32.490
Secretary David M. Gomez: informed of the President's

asr-000157
00:13:32.490 --> 00:13:34.290
Secretary David M. Gomez: activities in the country and his

asr-000158
00:13:34.290 --> 00:13:36.190
Secretary David M. Gomez: representation of national interest

asr-000159
00:13:36.670 --> 00:13:39.070
Secretary David M. Gomez: on the global stage.

asr-000160
00:13:39.070 --> 00:13:40.610
Secretary David M. Gomez: In addition,

asr-000161
00:13:40.770 --> 00:13:42.610
Secretary David M. Gomez: the program supports collaborative projects

asr-000162
00:13:42.610 --> 00:13:44.670
Secretary David M. Gomez: with other government agencies

asr-000163
00:13:44.670 --> 00:13:46.910
Secretary David M. Gomez: such as campaigns with the Department of Energy

asr-000164
00:13:46.910 --> 00:13:48.550
Secretary David M. Gomez: on Energy Conservation

asr-000165
00:13:48.550 --> 00:13:50.610
Secretary David M. Gomez: and Efficiency, which help bring

asr-000166
00:13:50.610 --> 00:13:52.750
Secretary David M. Gomez: national priorities closer to the people.

asr-000167
00:13:52.750 --> 00:13:54.290
Secretary David M. Gomez: This interagency effort

asr-000168
00:13:54.630 --> 00:13:56.510
Secretary David M. Gomez: demonstrates our commitment

asr-000169
00:13:56.510 --> 00:13:58.550
Secretary David M. Gomez: to a whole-of-government approach

asr-000170
00:13:58.550 --> 00:14:00.490
Secretary David M. Gomez: to communication, ensuring

asr-000171
00:14:00.490 --> 00:14:02.430
Secretary David M. Gomez: that important programs in

asr-000172
00:14:02.430 --> 00:14:04.410
Secretary David M. Gomez: energy, health, agriculture,

asr-000173
00:14:04.790 --> 00:14:06.810
Secretary David M. Gomez: social protection, and other key sectors

asr-000174
00:14:06.810 --> 00:14:08.510
Secretary David M. Gomez: are clearly communicated

asr-000175
00:14:08.510 --> 00:14:10.530
Secretary David M. Gomez: and well understood by the public.

asr-000176
00:14:11.570 --> 00:14:12.630
Secretary David M. Gomez: Ultimately, the

asr-000177
00:14:12.630 --> 00:14:14.110
Secretary David M. Gomez: Presidential Communications Program

asr-000178
00:14:14.110 --> 00:14:16.770
Secretary David M. Gomez: positions communication as a bridge

asr-000179
00:14:16.770 --> 00:14:18.710
Secretary David M. Gomez: between the government and the people,

asr-000180
00:14:18.870 --> 00:14:20.750
Secretary David M. Gomez: a bridge built

asr-000181
00:14:20.750 --> 00:14:22.190
Secretary David M. Gomez: on trust, transparency,

asr-000182
00:14:22.370 --> 00:14:24.530
Secretary David M. Gomez: and accountability. It ensures

asr-000183
00:14:24.530 --> 00:14:26.990
Secretary David M. Gomez: that the President's policies and administration's

asr-000184
00:14:26.990 --> 00:14:28.170
Secretary David M. Gomez: development agenda

asr-000185
00:14:28.170 --> 00:14:30.550
Secretary David M. Gomez: are not only heard, but also

asr-000186
00:14:30.550 --> 00:14:32.850
Secretary David M. Gomez: understood, embraced, and supported

asr-000187
00:14:32.850 --> 00:14:33.950
Secretary David M. Gomez: by the citizenry.

asr-000188
00:14:34.930 --> 00:14:36.090
Secretary David M. Gomez: Next slide, please.

asr-000189
00:14:37.110 --> 00:14:38.810
Secretary David M. Gomez: Next, we present the programs

asr-000190
00:14:38.810 --> 00:14:41.050
Secretary David M. Gomez: of the attached agencies of the PCO.

asr-000191
00:14:41.630 --> 00:14:43.190
Secretary David M. Gomez: First, under the PBS

asr-000192
00:14:43.190 --> 00:14:44.670
Secretary David M. Gomez: Bureau of Broadcast Services,

asr-000193
00:14:45.230 --> 00:14:47.070
Secretary David M. Gomez: we implement the Public Radio

asr-000194
00:14:47.070 --> 00:14:49.150
Secretary David M. Gomez: Broadcasting Program, which ensures

asr-000195
00:14:49.150 --> 00:14:50.810
Secretary David M. Gomez: nationwide access

asr-000196
00:14:50.810 --> 00:14:52.910
Secretary David M. Gomez: to timely and relevant information

asr-000197
00:14:52.910 --> 00:14:54.390
Secretary David M. Gomez: through radio.

asr-000198
00:14:55.150 --> 00:14:56.690
Secretary David M. Gomez: Second, the Bureau of

asr-000199
00:14:56.690 --> 00:14:59.010
Secretary David M. Gomez: Communication Services, or BCS,

asr-000201
00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:11.900
Secretary David M. Gomez: We carry out the government communications program which produces print, audiovisual, and digital materials that amplify government policies, projects, and services for public awareness and understanding.

asr-000202
00:15:13.260 --> 00:15:26.380
Secretary David M. Gomez: The News and Information Bureau is responsible for providing efficient, effective, productive, and economical services relating to the development and formulation of domestic and foreign information program of the government.

asr-000203
00:15:27.560 --> 00:15:28.780
Secretary David M. Gomez: Next slide, please.

asr-000204
00:15:30.200 --> 00:15:45.540
Secretary David M. Gomez: Fourth, the National Printing Office oversees the National Printing Program which provides high-security printing services for government agencies, ensuring integrity and efficiency in the production of accountable forms and other official documents.

