asr-002037
01:19:04.410 --> 01:19:06.010
Rep. Brian Poe: Kaya nagpapasalamat po ako.

asr-002038
01:19:06.010 --> 01:19:11.390
Rep. Brian Poe: And on that note, there are certain things that I want to point out regarding the budget.

asr-002039
01:19:11.570 --> 01:19:14.950
Rep. Brian Poe: First is regarding IBC -13's budget.

asr-002040
01:19:15.310 --> 01:19:17.450
Rep. Brian Poe: Tama po ba yung binabasa ko dito?

asr-002041
01:19:17.610 --> 01:19:27.750
Rep. Brian Poe: From 122 million pesos in the 2026 current program, it's now at zero pesos for 2027, correct po?

asr-002043
01:19:27.950 --> 01:19:28.670
Secretary David M. Gomez: That's correct, Your Honor.

asr-002042
01:19:28.970 --> 01:19:34.670
Rep. Brian Poe: Okay. So that's a 100% decrease in IBC-13's budget, tama?

asr-002044
01:19:34.670 --> 01:19:49.730
Rep. Brian Poe: Which is baffling to me because I feel that IBC 13 has been a critical partner in improving the trust and approval of government, especially of Congress.

asr-002045
01:19:50.510 --> 01:19:55.310
Rep. Brian Poe: I believe that recently, the surveys have shown that Congress's numbers

asr-002046
01:19:55.310 --> 01:19:57.570
Rep. Brian Poe: have gone up in terms of trust and approval

asr-002047
01:19:57.570 --> 01:20:02.790
Rep. Brian Poe: because there are many programs now in government that show the hard work of congressmen.

asr-002048
01:20:02.930 --> 01:20:04.010
Rep. Brian Poe: Tama po ba, Secretary?

asr-002049
01:20:04.010 --> 01:20:05.390
Rep. Brian Poe: I completely agree, Your Honor.

asr-002050
01:20:06.270 --> 01:20:10.290
Rep. Brian Poe: So, if that's the case, then why are we removing budget for a program that's working?

asr-002051
01:20:10.890 --> 01:20:13.630
Rep. Brian Poe: If not, we should be increasing the budget.

asr-002052
01:20:13.810 --> 01:20:15.970
Rep. Brian Poe: Madam Chair, just to give context to the committee,

asr-002053
01:20:16.210 --> 01:20:22.170
Rep. Brian Poe: because we should be benchmarking across ASEAN to see what our neighbors are spending.

asr-002054
01:20:22.630 --> 01:20:25.690
Rep. Brian Poe: Madam Chair, do you know how much Indonesia is spending

asr-002055
01:20:25.690 --> 01:20:31.530
Rep. Brian Poe: for their state media? For Televisi Republic Indonesia, it's roughly 4 billion pesos.

asr-002056
01:20:31.530 --> 01:20:36.310
Rep. Brian Poe: For Radio Republic Indonesia, it's 3 .4 billion pesos.

asr-002057
01:20:36.530 --> 01:20:40.770
Rep. Brian Poe: Here, we're only talking about hundreds of millions of pesos for our state media,

asr-002058
01:20:40.930 --> 01:20:42.990
Rep. Brian Poe: and we can't even give it to them, Madam Chair.

asr-002059
01:20:43.530 --> 01:20:49.710
Rep. Brian Poe: Which is why I wanted to point this glaring decrease in the budget of our communications.

asr-002060
01:20:50.610 --> 01:20:54.510
Rep. Brian Poe: The other thing I wanted to point out is that there was a request,

asr-002061
01:20:54.510 --> 01:20:56.390
Rep. Brian Poe: Although I don't think it was granted,

asr-002062
01:20:56.690 --> 01:21:07.950
Rep. Brian Poe: that the IBC budget be an additional 479 million for personnel, MOE, and even Kong TV programs.

asr-002063
01:21:08.170 --> 01:21:09.330
Rep. Brian Poe: Is this correct, Mr. Secretary?

asr-002064
01:21:10.110 --> 01:21:11.550
Secretary David M. Gomez: I believe so, Your Honor, yes.

asr-002065
01:21:12.410 --> 01:21:16.310
Rep. Brian Poe: Why do we need money for personnel and maintenance and operations?

asr-002066
01:21:16.590 --> 01:21:17.890
Rep. Brian Poe: Can you talk about that a little bit?

asr-002067
01:21:17.890 --> 01:21:19.870
Secretary David M. Gomez: Thank you very much.

asr-002068
